// Rstest Snapshot v1

exports[`the wire's catalogue > global_background_only: the message 1`] = `
"The global \`ReadableStream\` is not defined on the main thread: Lynx has it on the background thread only.

Use it in code that runs on the background, such as an effect or an event handler, or call such code from a main-thread function with \`runOnBackground\`.
https://sohedra.com/e/global_background_only"
`;

exports[`the wire's catalogue > global_not_filled: the message 1`] = `
"The global \`URL\` is not defined: Lynx's engine doesn't have it, and no import put it there.

Import "@sohedra/lynx-polyfill/url" in the first line of the app's entry, or "@sohedra/lynx-polyfill", which holds it too.
https://sohedra.com/e/global_not_filled"
`;

exports[`the wire's catalogue > global_not_on_lynx: the message 1`] = `
"The global \`crypto\` is not defined: Lynx's engine doesn't have it, and no fill gives it.

For hashes, use a library in plain JavaScript such as @noble/hashes.
https://sohedra.com/e/global_not_on_lynx"
`;

exports[`the wire's catalogue > page_already_mounted: the message 1`] = `
"A second call of \`mountPage\` did nothing: the page the first call started still runs.
Seen on the main thread.

Call \`mountPage\` once, in the page's entry. To show a component over the page, call \`mount\`; to show another page, change what the root component shows.
https://sohedra.com/e/page_already_mounted"
`;

exports[`the wire's catalogue > page_reloaded_on_one_thread: the message 1`] = `
"This page reloaded on one of its threads only.
Seen on the main thread: it shows load 1 of the page and got a message of load 2.

Reload the page through Lynx, with \`lynx.reload()\` or the host's reload, so both threads start the new page together.
https://sohedra.com/e/page_reloaded_on_one_thread"
`;

exports[`the wire's catalogue > threads_from_different_builds: the message 1`] = `
"This page's main thread and background thread come from different builds of the app.
Seen on the main thread: it reads version 1 of what the threads send each other, and got version 2.

Build the app again and reopen the page, so both threads load from one build. If the host caches bundles, clear its cache.
https://sohedra.com/e/threads_from_different_builds"
`;

exports[`the wire's catalogue > value_not_copyable: the message 1`] = `
"A value sent to the main thread cannot be copied (Do not know how to serialize a BigInt).

Send plain data: strings, numbers, booleans, null, arrays and plain objects, without cycles or BigInt values.
https://sohedra.com/e/value_not_copyable"
`;
